/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 76 0 R
/T (Honeypot Isolation: The service runs on a dedicated port \(8888\) with no access to real production data, healthcare records, or system resources. No Payload Execution: The socket listener only reads the first 1024 bytes \(optional\) and  never executes any received data. Deception Integrity: The deceptive message does not reveal the true nature of the system  \(no "honeypot" text, only realistic healthcare error messages\). Log Integrity: JSON threat logs are append-only; no modification or deletion capability is  exposed via the network. Dashboard Exposure: The dashboard \(port 5001\) binds to localhost only by default. In  production healthcare environments, it must be behind a reverse proxy with authentication.)
/E (Honeypot Isolation: The service runs on a dedicated port \(8888\) with no access to real production data, healthcare records, or system resources. No Payload Execution: The socket listener only reads the first 1024 bytes \(optional\) and  never executes any received data. Deception Integrity: The deceptive message does not reveal the true nature of the system  \(no "honeypot" text, only realistic healthcare error messages\). Log Integrity: JSON threat logs are append-only; no modification or deletion capability is  exposed via the network. Dashboard Exposure: The dashboard \(port 5001\) binds to localhost only by default. In  production healthcare environments, it must be behind a reverse proxy with authentication.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 76 0 R
/T (Concurrent Connections: Support at least 50 simultaneous TCP connections using Python threads \(simulating DDoS or scanning\). Log Write Latency: < 10 ms per threat log entry \(excluding disk I/O\). Dashboard Response Time: < 200 ms for /api/threats with up to 10,000 log entries. Resource Limits: CPU usage < 5% idle, Memory < 50 MB under normal attack load. Uptime: Designed to run continuously for 30+ days without restart in healthcare SOC environments.)
/E (Concurrent Connections: Support at least 50 simultaneous TCP connections using Python threads \(simulating DDoS or scanning\). Log Write Latency: < 10 ms per threat log entry \(excluding disk I/O\). Dashboard Response Time: < 200 ms for /api/threats with up to 10,000 log entries. Resource Limits: CPU usage < 5% idle, Memory < 50 MB under normal attack load. Uptime: Designed to run continuously for 30+ days without restart in healthcare SOC environments.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [14]
>>
